title: Cutting the fuse
story: fernhill
continues: folly
description: The winning branch out of the folly — cut the cord, then open the
  box with the locket. Both tool gates need the explicit `with` phrasing.

---

# The shears came from the Kitchen in vine.transcript, the locket out of the
# vine. Both are required below and both are in hand.
> inventory
[OK: contains "garden shears"]
[OK: contains "silver locket"]

# `cuttable with the garden shears` — but the instrument must be NAMED. Holding
# the only tool that works is not enough; see fuse-lose.transcript for what the
# bare `cut the fuse` does instead.
> cut the fuse with the garden shears
[OK: contains "The shears bite through the waxed cord"]
[OK: contains "dies a hand's breadth from the cache"]

# The turn phrase stops with the fuse — `on every turn while it is lit` no
# longer holds, and the three-turn kill never arrives.
> look
[OK: not contains "Sparks walk the waxed cord"]
[OK: not contains "The fuse hisses on"]
[OK: contains "Soot still ghosts the walls in here"]

# `openable with the silver locket` — the same explicit-instrument rule.
> open the deed box with the silver locket
[OK: contains "You open the deed box"]
[OK: contains "Inside the deed box you see deed"]

# Now that the box is open, `deed` resolves to the deed rather than the box,
# and the message says which container it came out of.
> take the deed
[OK: contains "You take the deed from the deed box"]
[STATE: true, player.inventory contains deed]

> read the deed
[OK: contains "held in perpetuity by the family and heirs of the bearer"]

# nerve (5) + recovered (10) on top of the 20 carried in: 35.
> score
[OK: contains "You have scored 35 out of 50"]
